          "createdAt": "2026-02-05T11:43:15.127Z",
          "description": "# Description\n\nAs a product manager or operations team member, I should be able to manage asset tag associations through a Retool interface so that I can add or remove tags from assets without writing code or using CLI tools.\n\nRetool to update: [https://retoolv3.anchorage-development.com/apps/58d84db4-acc0-11ef-8293-8bca805579cf/Asset%20types](\u003chttps://retoolv3.anchorage-development.com/apps/58d84db4-acc0-11ef-8293-8bca805579cf/Asset%2520types\u003e)\n\n# **Acceptance Criteria**\n\n* Reuse the assets listing page in Retool (use the edit box to manage tags)\n  * Note: Edit box is currently not in use\n* Page shows searchable list of all assets with their current tags\n* User can select an asset from the list or search by asset ID/name\n* ~~For selected asset, UI displays:~~\n  * ~~Asset details (ID, name, network, token type) (nice to have)~~\n  * Current tags with visual badges\n  * Available tags to add (from tag definitions)\n* \"Add Tag\" functionality:\n  * Dropdown/multi-select to choose tag(s) from available tags\n  * \"Add\" button calls `AddTagsToAsset` gRPC endpoint\n  * Success message shows updated tag list\n  * Error handling with user-friendly messages\n* \"Remove Tag\" functionality:\n  * Each tag badge has \"X\" remove button\n  * Confirmation dialog before removal\n  * \"Remove\" action calls `RemoveTagsFromAsset` gRPC endpoint\n  * Success message shows updated tag list\n  * Error handling with user-friendly messages\n* ~~Authorization is enforced (must be in ~~`~~asset-tag-editors~~`~~ group)~~\n* ~~UI shows permission denied error for unauthorized users~~\n* Tag changes are logged and visible in audit trail\n* Manual testing checklist completed with screenshots\n* UI is accessible via standard Retool deployment URL\n\n# **Dependencies**\n\nNone",
